---
import Doc from '../../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Pager from '../../../components/Pager.astro';
const slug = 'concepts/pruner';
---
<Doc slug={slug} title="Context: checkpoints and the explorer">
  <h1>Context: checkpoints and the explorer</h1>
  <p class="lede">Finish real work in a 20–30K token context, with one rule: cheap models read; the main model decides.</p>

  <h2>Checkpoints</h2>
  <p>
    The agent chooses what stays in its own context with the <code>checkpoint</code> tool: keep a
    result whole, keep only some of its lines, or replace it with a one-line note. Everything
    dropped stays in the session log and comes back with <code>recall</code>. The agent calls it
    when a step is done, and the runtime asks for one when the context reaches the trigger
    (axon's <code>pruner.mode</code>: low 48K, moderate 32K, extreme 20K tokens). Asked of the main
    model, a checkpoint reuses the cached prompt, so it costs about one ordinary step. If the work
    really needs more, the agent keeps it and the next checkpoint waits for growth beyond that.
  </p>
  <pre><code># optional; omit to let the main model decide checkpoints
pruner:
  model: some/other-model
  provider: openrouter   # defaults to the main provider if omitted</code></pre>

  <h2>The explorer</h2>
  <p>
    With <code>explorer.model</code> set, the agent gets an <code>explore</code> tool. It hands a broad
    question to a cheaper model that may only read and search, in its own throw-away context. The
    explorer reports facts with quotes; every quote is checked against the file, and only verified
    facts reach the agent, labelled as the explorer's reading. The agent still reads raw whatever
    it edits.
  </p>
  <pre><code>explorer:
  model: z-ai/glm-5.3-flash
  provider: openrouter</code></pre>

  <h2>Auditing</h2>
  <p>
    Both side models are tapped into the <a href="/cortex/docs/concepts/trace-log/">trace log</a>
    next to the main one, so you can read what a checkpoint kept and what the explorer read.
    Choices made with <code>/pruner</code> and <code>/explorer</code>, or in the editor, are saved to
    your user config.
  </p>

  <div class="callout info">
    <span class="ico">📖</span>
    <div class="callout-body">
      <strong>The mechanism is axon's.</strong> See axon's <code>WORKING_CONTEXT.md</code> for the
      design and its guarantees. The free review pool (<code>pruner.models</code>) is retired; an old
      config still loads and says so.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-pager"><Pager slug={slug} /></div>
</Doc>
